  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "Some amount of a radioactive substance (half-life <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math>&nbsp;days ) is spread inside a room and consequently, the level of radiation becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn></math> times the permissible level&nbsp;for normal occupancy of the room. After how many days will the room be safe for occupation?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "lCBHD",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn></math> days",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "rfh5q",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>34</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></math> days",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ynYZ0",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>56</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></math> days",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "1DP7s",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>62</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn></math> days",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>since, the initial activity is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn></math>&nbsp;times the activity for safe occupancy, therefore <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>N</mi></math>.<br />since, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>&#8733;</mo><mi>N</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>50</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mn>10</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><mn>50</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><mn>50</mn></mrow><msubsup><mi>log</mi><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>699</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>301</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;days</p>",
